# 0009. Jupyter notebooks: jupytext, molten and image.nvim

- Status: Accepted
- Date: 2026-11-07

## Context
Notebooks (`.ipynb`) should open, run and be edited in Neovim with normal Python tooling.

## Decision
- jupytext.nvim opens a notebook as a `# %%` percent-format Python script and writes it back on
  save, keeping outputs. It loads at start because it owns `BufReadCmd *.ipynb`.
- molten-nvim runs cells in a real Jupyter kernel; image.nvim draws plots via the kitty graphics
  protocol (Ghostty/kitty).
- molten runs on a dedicated python host, `~/.local/share/nvim/python-host` (`make notebook`);
  project kernels are registered with `make kernel VENV=…`.
- Cell helpers and keys (`<leader>j`, `]j`/`[j`) live in `lua/config/notebook.lua`.

## Alternatives
Not recorded at the time.

## Rationale
The notebook is plain Python in the buffer, so pyright, completion and formatting work unchanged.

## Consequences
- molten's commands come from `:UpdateRemotePlugins`; it must not get a `cmd` lazy trigger.
- Needs `uv`, a python host per machine, and tmux `allow-passthrough on` for images.

## References
- `lua/plugins/notebook.lua`, `lua/config/notebook.lua`, commit `b3e8202`
